      "title": "Host-memory transfer rate over a direct Thunderbolt 4 link, 16 MiB, by direction",
      "summary": "Grouped horizontal bars. Linux to Mac: TBCCL 15.5 Gbit/s, iperf3 single stream 15.81 Gbit/s. Mac to Linux: TBCCL 18.3 Gbit/s, iperf3 single stream 18.81 Gbit/s. The two programs agree within about 3 percent in both directions, and the Mac to Linux direction is faster in both. These are TCP goodput through two operating-system kernels, not the Thunderbolt 4 link rate.",
      "conditions": "One completion-confirmed 16 MiB message at a time, host memory, TCP/IPv4 over IP over Thunderbolt, MTU 9000, TBCCL 0.6.0, one pair of machines. The iperf3 bars are a single TCP stream (receiver goodput).",
