      "id": "native-staging",
      "title": "Completion time of a 16 MiB transfer by memory path, Linux (CUDA) to Mac (Metal)",
      "summary": "Horizontal bars, lower is better. Host memory control 8,667 microseconds. CUDA pinned memory to Metal shared memory with synchronous staging 9,968 microseconds, which is 1,301 more than the control. Asynchronous chunked staging with 256 KiB chunks at depth 2 took 8,677 microseconds, equal to the control, so the staging was overlapped with the transfer. This shows an overlap benefit in completion time; it is not direct device-to-device DMA.",
      "conditions": "16 MiB, completion-confirmed, A to B, TBCCL 0.6.0 over TCP/IPv4. Both device paths stage through host memory; there is no direct CUDA-to-Metal DMA. Submitting an asynchronous operation returns in microseconds and says nothing about completion; the bars are completion times.",
      "page": "native-results.md",
      "section": "Device memory",
      "statistic": "medians over 3 independent repetitions; the whisker is the minimum to maximum over those repetitions",
